[? if scps_urgency <= 1 and scps_seats >= 15 : The rapid rise in SCPS votes is extremely worrying. Many had believed that the party was moribund; now, some of us consider it to be the greatest threat to democracy in Saskatchewan. ?]

[? if anti_democratic_coalition >= 50 : Together, the anti-democratic CPC(S), SCPS, and SCPS have a majority in the Assembly. A stable governing majority will be almost impossible. ?]

There are some potential coalition arrangements.

@coalition_menu

- @ccf_majority: We have achieved a Majority!
- @ccf_minority: Attempt to continue on as a Minority government
- @coalition_options: What are our options regarding coalitions?
- @supply_confidence_options: Could we seek Supply and Confidence?
- @socred_plurality: Social Credit wins a Plurality
- @socred_majority: Social Credit wins a Majority
- @liberal_plurality: The Liberals win a Plurality
- @liberal_majority: The Liberals win a Majority
- @tory_plurality: The Tories win a Plurality
- @tory_majority: The Tories win a Majority
- @cooperative_coalition: Impossible, wtf?

# TODO: black-brown coalition

# Custom Coalitions here:

@ccf_forms_government
on-arrival: {! 
Q.premier = Q.ccf_leader; 
Q.premier_party = party_names.ccf; 
Q.premier_img = Q.premier_portraits[Q.ccf_leader];
!}

@socred_forms_government
on-arrival: {! 
Q.premier = Q.scps_leader; 
Q.premier_party = party_names.scps; 
Q.premier_img = Q.premier_portraits[Q.scps_leader];
!}

@lps_forms_government
on-arrival: {! 
Q.premier = Q.lps_leader; 
Q.premier_party = party_names.lps; 
Q.premier_img = Q.premier_portraits[Q.lps_leader];
!}

@cps_forms_government
on-arrival: {! 
Q.premier = Q.cps_leader; 
Q.premier_party = party_names.cps; 
Q.premier_img = Q.premier_portraits[Q.cps_leader];
!}

@ccf_majority
title: We have achieved a majority!
view-if: ccf_seats >= seat_majority
on-arrival: ccf_in_government = 1; in_ccf_majority = 1; pro_republic += 5; foreign_minister_party = party_names.ccf; foreign_minister = "Williams"; interior_minister_party = party_names.ccf; interior_minister = "Brockelbank"; justice_minister_party = party_names.ccf; justice_minister = "Underhill"; labour_minister_party = party_names.ccf; labour_minister = "Carlyle"; rcmp_minister_party = party_names.ccf; rcmp_minister = "Leber"; economic_minister_party = party_names.ccf; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; finance_minister_party = party_names.ccf; finance_minister = "Nicholson"; agriculture_minister_party = party_names.ccf; agriculture_minister = "Wright"; rcmp_loyalty -= 0.05; 
call: ccf_forms_government
go-to: ministries

We have achieved a majority of seats. We can now govern in a stable capacity for up to five years. 


@ccf_minority
title: Could we rule in a minority?
view-if: ccf_seats <= seat_majority and largest_party = party_names.ccf
on-arrival: premier = ccf_leader; premier_party = party_names.ccf; ccf_in_government = 1; in_ccf_majority = 1; pro_republic += 5; foreign_minister_party = party_names.ccf; foreign_minister = "Williams"; interior_minister_party = party_names.ccf; interior_minister = "Brockelbank"; justice_minister_party = party_names.ccf; justice_minister = "Underhill"; labour_minister_party = party_names.ccf; labour_minister = "Carlyle"; rcmp_minister_party = party_names.ccf; rcmp_minister = "Leber"; economic_minister_party = party_names.ccf; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; finance_minister_party = party_names.ccf; finance_minister = "Nicholson"; agriculture_minister_party = party_names.ccf; agriculture_minister = "Wright"; rcmp_loyalty -= 0.05; 

We have achieved a plurality of the vote. For one reason or another, we can choose to continue as a minority government, negotiating with parties on a bill by bill basis.


@coalition_options
title: Coalition Options

- @ccf_tory_coalition
- @ccf_socred_coalition
- @election.coalition_menu: Return


@ccf_tory_coalition
title: Could we coalition with the Tories?
unavailable-subtitle: They do not trust us enough
choose-if: cps_relation >= 60 and (cps_ideology == 'Red Toryism' or cps_leader == 'James Anderson') and (ccf_ideology == 'Social Democracy' or ccf_ideology == 'Progressivism')
call: election.ccf_forms_government

@ccf_socred_coalition
title: Could we coalition with Social Credit?
unavailable-subtitle: The Socreds are unwilling to coalition with us
choose-if: scps_relation >= 70 and ccf_ideology == 'Social Democracy' or ccf_ideology == 'Progressivism'
call: election.ccf_forms_government


@supply_confidence_options
title: What are our options for Supply and Confidence?

We could seek the support of another party in a Supply and Confidence Agreement; guaranteeing policy concessions for a vote with us against non-confidence motions. 

- @ccf_tory_sc: Could we enter into an S&C Agreement with the Tories?
- @ccf_socred_sc: Could we enter into an S&C Agreement with the SoCreds?
- @election.coalition_menu: Return

@ccf_tory_sc
title: Tory Supply and Confidence
subtitle: The Red Tories are pulling their clout
unavailable-subtitle: They do not trust us enough
choose-if: cps_relation >= 40 and cps_ideology == 'Red Toryism'
call: election.ccf_forms_government

The Tories have agreed to enter into a Supply and Confidence agreement. [? if cps_leader == 'John Diefenbaker' : John Diefenbaker's Red Toryism remains markedly economically interventionist and therefore, friendly to our own policies. ?]

@ccf_socred_sc
title: S&C with Socreds
choose-if: scps_relation >= 60
subtitle: The Socreds are, surprisingly, willing to enter an S&A agreement
unavailable-subtitle: The Socreds are unwilling to negotiate 
call: election.ccf_forms_government

The Social Credit Party has agreed to enter into a Supply and Confidence agreement with us. 

@socred_plurality
view-if: largest_party == 'SCPS' and scps_seats <= seat_majority
call: election.socred_forms_government


@socred_majority
title: Social Credit wins a Majority Government
view-if: scps_seats >= seat_majority
call: election.socred_forms_government
on-arrival: {!
    for (var p of Q.parties) {
        Q[p + '_in_government'] = 0;
    }
    Q.scps_in_government = 1; 
!}

@liberal_plurality
view-if: largest_party == 'LPS' and lps_seats <= seat_majority
call: election.lps_forms_government

The LPS does not maintain strong enough relations with any one party to form a majority governing coalition. Therefore, they will attempt to organize a minority government and receieve support on an ad hoc basis. 


@liberal_majority
title: The Liberals win a Majority Government
view-if: lps_seats >= seat_majority
call: election.lps_forms_government
on-arrival: {!
    for (var p of Q.parties) {
        Q[p + '_in_government'] = 0;
    }
    Q.lps_in_government = 1; 
!}

The LPS has achieved a majority. For the next 4-5 years, the LPS will be essentially free to do as they please in Saskatchewan. 

- @root: Buggers

@tory_plurality
title: The Tories win a Plurality
view-if: largest_party == 'CPS' and cps_seats <= seat_majority
call: election.cps_forms_government
on-arrival: {!
    for (var p of Q.parties) {
        Q[p + '_in_government'] = 0;
    }
    Q.cps_in_government = 1; 
!}

@tory_majority
title: The Tories win a Majority
view-if: cps_seats >= seat_majority
call: election.cps_forms_government
on-arrival: {!
    for (var p of Q.parties) {
        Q[p + '_in_government'] = 0;
    }
    Q.cps_in_government = 1; 
!}


@cooperative_coalition
title: A traditional alliance
subtitle: CPS + PPS ([+ cooperative_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: CPS + PPS ([+ cooperative_coalition +]%)
view-if: cooperative_coalition >= 50
choose-if: cooperative_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: ccf_in_government = 0; ccf_toleration = 0; foreign_minister_party = "CPS"; interior_minister_party = "CPS"; justice_minister_party = "CPS"; labour_minister_party = "PPS"; rcmp_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "CPS"; finance_minister_party = "CPS"; agriculture_minister_party = "CPS"; in_cooperative_coalition = 1;

# Haha, not happening

Anderson's Cooperative Coalition has managed to attain another majority. 

- @anderson_premier: Anderson holds steady

@anderson_premier
on-arrival: premier =  "James Anderson"; premier_party = "CPS"; ccf_in_government = 0; in_ccf_majority = 0; 


@new_elections
on-arrival: {!
Q.next_parl_election_month = Q.month + 3;
Q.next_election_time = Q.time + 3;
if (Q.next_parl_election_month > 12) {
    Q.next_parl_election_month -= 12;
    Q.next_parl_election_year = Q.year + 1;
} else {
    Q.next_parl_election_year = Q.year;
}
if (Q.premier == "Brüning") {
    Q.pps_relation -= 5;
    Q.cps_relation -= 5;
}
Q.pro_republic -= 8;
Q.workers_ccf -= 5;
Q.new_middle_ccf -= 5;
Q.old_middle_ccf -= 5;
Q.farmers_ccf -= 5;
Q.catholics_ccf -= 3;
Q.new_middle_cps -= 8;
Q.old_middle_cps -= 8;
Q.new_middle_lps -= 5;
Q.old_middle_lps -= 10;
Q.farmers_scps -= 5;
Q.workers_scps += 5;
Q.old_middle_scps += 6;
Q.new_middle_scps += 6;
Q.farmers_scps += 6;
Q.unemployed_scps += 5;
// Thresholds are kind of arbitrary - adjusted because of negative economic effects on pro_republic
if (Q.pro_republic < 45 && Q.pro_republic >= 36) {
    Q.workers_ccf -= 6;
}
if (Q.pro_republic < 36) {
    // TODO: if you pursue a consistently revolutionary course, you might avoid this? But you might also cause a coalition between Needham and the PPS.
    Q.pps_relation -= 5;
    Q.cps_relation -= 5;
    Q.workers_ccf *= 0.85;
    Q.unemployed_ccf -= 2;
    Q.new_middle_ccf -= 5;
    Q.old_middle_ccf -= 5;
    Q.farmers_ccf -= 5;
    Q.catholics_ccf -= 3;
    Q.workers_scps += 8;
    Q.old_middle_scps += 8;
    Q.new_middle_scps += 8;
    Q.farmers_scps += 8;
    Q.unemployed_scps += 8;   
}
if (Q.scps_majority >= 50) {
    Q.ful_strength += 100;
    Q.kkk_strength += 100;
    Q.coup_progress += 3;
}
!}

There is no path to a workable Assembly majority or minority government. The next elections are set for [+ next_parl_election_month : month +] [+ next_parl_election_year +].

The people's faith in democracy is shaken by this ordeal. Of course, the SCPSs are exploiting the instability to claim that democracy is unworkable, and that Saskatchewan needs a strong leader.


@new_elections_ccf
on-arrival: next_election_time = time+3; next_parl_election_month = month + 3; next_parl_election_year = year; next_parl_election_year = year + 1 if next_parl_election_month > 12; next_parl_election_month = next_parl_election_month - 12 if next_parl_election_month > 12; new_middle_ccf -= 5; old_middle_ccf -= 5; workers_ccf -= 3; catholics_ccf -= 3; in_election = 1

Since the remaining bourgeois and right-wing parties cannot form a tolerable governing agreement, new elections have been called for [+ next_parl_election_month : month +] [+ next_parl_election_year +]. The previous premier has resigned, and has been replaced by Heinrich Brüning, also of the PPS Party, ruling as part of a prime ministerial cabinet. 

We are seen as responsible for the failure to form a government, and many of our middle-class and even some working-class supporters have deserted the party.


@ministries

We can pick from any number of ministries. Controlling a ministry allows us to directly effect policy in that area. [? if in_left_front : Any ministry that we do not take will be given to the CPC(S). ?] [? if in_left_front and rcmp_minister_party == "CPC(S)" : If the CPC(S) controls the RCMP Ministry, the army will most likely revolt. ?]

- #mins_1928
- #drop_mins_1928


@cooperatives
title: Cooperative Ministry
subtitle: A new ministry to oversee the cooperatives. 
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 5
view-if: cooperatives_minister_party != party_names.ccf
on-arrival: leverage -= 5; cooperatives_minister_party = party_names.ccf; cooperatives_minister = "Carlyle"
go-to: ministries

@education
title: Education Ministry
subtitle: Saskatchewan has many issues in education, and we should be in a position to address them.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 5
view-if: education_minister_party != party_names.ccf
on-arrival: leverage -= 5; education_minister_party = party_names.ccf; education_minister = "Carlyle"
go-to: ministries

@mineral_resoures
title: Mineral Resources Ministry
subtitle: Saskatchewan has many untapped natural resources that we could use to our advantage.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
